hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27633","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: Haddathana al-Mas'udi, he said: Ma'bad ibn Khalid narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Qutaylah bint Sayfi al-Juhaniyyah, she said: A scholar of the rabbis came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Muhammad, good people are you, were it not that you associate. He said: Glory be to Allah, and what is that? He said: You say when you swear: By the Ka'bah. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waited a while, then he said: He has spoken, so whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: O Muhammad, good people are you, were it not that you set up a rival to Allah. He said: Glory be to Allah, and what is that? He said: You say: What Allah wills and you will. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, waited a while, then he said: He has spoken, so whoever says: What Allah wills, let him separate between them, then: you will."
